/ One save button for the desktop, which the form-dirty controller enables.
  Disabled from the start, as the form-dirty controller sets it on connect.
  Else it shows enabled until the controller connects. A phone has the save
  button in the title bar instead (see Ui::TitleBar::Component).

  The save button comes first in the form, because Enter in a field submits
  with the first submit button. The delete button moves to the left edge with
  order-first.
.flex.items-center.justify-end.gap-3.mt-6.max-lg:hidden
  button class=BUTTON_CLASS type="submit" disabled=true data-form-dirty-submit=true
    = icon 'check'
    = label
  - if delete_path
    = render Button::Component.new icon: 'trash',
                                   type: :submit,
                                   style: :secondary,
                                   options: { \
                                     **delete_options,
                                     title: t('crud.delete'),
                                     data: { turbo_confirm: t('crud.confirm_delete'), controller: 'tooltip' },
                                     class: 'order-first mr-auto text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 hover:text-orange-500 dark:hover:text-orange-500',
                                   }
/ A phone has the delete button as a red line of its own below the fields
- if delete_path
  .mt-8.lg:hidden
    = button_tag t('crud.delete'),
                 type: :submit,
                 **delete_options,
                 data: { turbo_confirm: t('crud.confirm_delete') },
                 class: 'w-full rounded-xl py-3 text-headline bg-white text-signal-negative active:bg-gray-200 dark:bg-slate-800/60 dark:active:bg-slate-700/60 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-red-500'
